    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d103">

                <pb facs="0210" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/1949: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-01T13:00:00+08:00">October 1, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 1—6:09 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>686. Your 355, September 30, 6 p.m.,<anchor n="86" xml:id="d103-f1"/> last
                    sentence. While train service is maintained to Mukden, it is not very safe. The
                    only telegraphic communication is via Dairen by Japanese lines. The Chinese
                    wireless to Harbin is functioning.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
